      "math_academy_id": "q-124953",
      "knowledge_point_id": "566f4fc1-ba4d-5433-9812-a3f5470e3d1e",
      "knowledge_point": "Computing a Probability Over an Interval Containing a Greater Than Symbol",
      "problem": "Given that the discrete random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function $F(x)$ shown in the table below, compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$\n\n| $x$ | $1.5$ | $2.5$ | $3.5$ | $4.5$ | $5.5$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $F(x)$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ | $\\frac{3}{8}$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{5}{8}$ | $1$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nHere, we want to compute $P(X\\ge 5.5).$ However, this interval is stated in the form $X\\ge 5.5,$ not $X>5.5.$\n\nSo first, we must convert the interval $X\\ge 5.5$ to the form $X>a.$ Looking at the given possible values of $X,$ we see that $X\\ge 5.5$ is equivalent to $X>4.5.$\n\nTherefore, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5.5) & =P(X>4.5) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4.5) \\\\  & =1-F(4.5) \\\\  & =1-\\frac{5}{8} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
